{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfUStSp5drcRdWniviNUX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Add the shift, hold off on the roaster — for now.**\n\nThe core issue is that your demand signal isn't solid enough to justify $103,000 in irreversible capex: two of your largest wholesale accounts are month-to-month, meaning a meaningful chunk of the \"20% growth\" you're solving for could disappear with 30 days' notice. A second shift is the reversible bet that matches the size of the problem you've actually confirmed (you're selling out weeks, not months), while a 35kg roaster is a step-change in capacity that only makes sense if the growth is durable.\n\nThe numbers back this up too: $103,000 upfront buys you roughly 24 months of second-shift labor ($4,200/mo). If demand holds and you've converted those wholesale accounts to firmer commitments (annual contracts, minimum volumes) within 6–12 months, that's your trigger to revisit the roaster purchase — at that point you'll also have better data on whether the 15kg machine's accelerated wear (and the ceiling of a second shift) is actually your binding constraint, rather than guessing now.\n\nThe one thing worth watching: if the second shift alone still can't clear the backlog, that's a stronger signal than the revenue growth number alone that you're structurally undercapacitized — worth re-running this call then."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16587,"cache_read_input_tokens":24048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16587},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7418558c-dc1d-4695-bf8c-1eaedcca05c9","uuid":"7af393aa-f07b-48f9-aafb-47906dea35d0","timestamp":"2026-